      "Indication | LV dysfunction with mild CAD.",
      "Findings | Increased indexed LVEDV and LVESV with LVEF of 27%. No LV hypertrophy is seen. Diffuse severe global hypokinesia is seen with preserved wall thickness.Normal indexed RVEDV and increased indexed RVESV with RVEF of 32%. No RV hypertrophy. Diffuse hypokinesia is seen with no dyskinesia/ aneurysmal out pouching.   Dilated LA (iLA vol – 53 ml/m2) with mild MR (RF 10-15%). Mildly dilated RA (iRA vol – 40 ml/m2) with mild TR (RF 15-20%).   T2 STIR images reveal no myocardial edema with normal T2 values (49 ms).On delayed enhancement imaging, near transmural LGE is seen in basal anteroseptal segment. Sub epicardial LGE is seen in inferior/ inferolateral segments of basal cavity, mid and apical lateral wall and the RV side of septum. LV myocardial fibrotic burden of 8%. No LV thrombus.  T1 mapping reveals increased LV myocardial native T1 values (1048 ms).CT correlation of lungs reveals few tiny sub pleural solid nodules scattered in both lungs. No significant mediastinal adenopathy is seen. Compression fracture is seen in visualized D8 vertebral body.",
      "(See graphs for BSA indexed LV/RV values)",
      " | EDV (mL) | ESV (mL) | SV (mL) | EF (%) | Mass (g)",
      "LV | 217 | 159 | 58 | 27 | 122",
      "RV | 194 | 132 | 63 | 32 | -",
      "Conclusion | Dilated LV with LVEF of 27%. Early dilated RV with RVEF of 32%.Sub epicardial to near transmural fibrosis in basal, mid and apical cavity as mentioned.CMR features are of non-ischemic dilated cardiomyopathy, s/o post myocarditis sequelae/ sarcoidosis. No myocardial inflammation at present.",
      "CARDIAC MAGNETIC RESONANCE IMAGING (CMR)",
      "Indication | Triple vessel disease for viability assessment.",
      "Findings | Few PVCs are seen during study period.Normal indexed LVEDV and increased indexed LVESV with LVEF of 45%. No LV hypertrophy is seen. Severe hypokinesia is seen in basal inferior/ anterolateral segments, mid anterior wall/ septum/ inferior segment, entire apical cavity and apex.The RV is normal in appearance with fair systolic function.   Dilated LA (iLA vol – 42 ml/m2) with mild MR (RF 10-15%). Normal RA dimension is seen with trivial TR. Focal separation of LV myocardium from the mitral annulus for a distance of 7 mm is seen from 3-6 o'clock position, s/o mitral annular disjunction. Mild prolapse of the anterior mitral leaflet into LA for a distance of 2 mm is seen.On delayed enhancement imaging, sub endocardial LGE is seen in basal inferior/ anterolateral segments, mid anterior wall/ septum/ inferior segment, entire apical cavity and apex. Diffuse LGE of the LV papillary muscles also seen. No LV thrombus.  Lungs and mediastinum are normal.",
      "(See graphs for BSA indexed LV values)",
      " | EDV (mL) | ESV (mL) | SV (mL) | EF (%) | Mass",
      "LV | 153 | 85 | 68 | 45 | 89",
      "Conclusion | Early dilated LV with LVEF of 45%. Sub endocardial infarcts in basal inferior/ anterolateral segments, mid anterior wall/ septum/ inferior segment, entire apical cavity and apex.Focal mitral annular disjunction with mild prolapse of anterior mitral leaflet.CMR features are of ischemic early dilated cardiomyopathy. Of the 17 segments, 12 are viable and rest are normal.",
      "CARDIAC MAGNETIC RESONANCE IMAGING (CMR)",
      "Indication | Hypertrophic cardiomyopathy for evaluation.",
      "Findings | Normal indexed LVEDV and LVESV with LVEF of 71%. Asymmetric hypertrophy of the LV is seen predominantly involving the anterior and anteroseptal segments with mid anterior segment measuring 22 mm in maximum end diastolic wall thickness. No SAM of the anterior mitral leaflet/ narrowing of the LVOT is seen. No regional wall motion abnormality is seen.The RV is normal in appearance with preserved systolic function. No RV hypertrophy.  Normal LA dimension (iLA vol – 37 ml/m2) is seen with mild MR (RF 15-20%). Normal right atrial dimensions with trivial TR is seen.T2 FS images reveal no myocardial edema with normal T2 values (52 ms).On delayed enhancement imaging, no LV myocardial/ papillary muscle LGE is seen. No LV thrombus. T1 mapping reveals diffusely raised native T1 values in the hypertrophied segments (1044 ms).Lungs are normal. Enlarged right paratracheal and subcarinal lymph nodes are seen measuring 14 mm in short axis.",
      "(See graphs for BSA indexed LV values)",
      " | EDV (mL) | ESV (mL) | SV (mL) | EF (%) | Mass",
      "LV | 131 | 39 | 92 | 71 | 116",
      "Conclusion | Non-dilated LV with LVEF of 71%.Asymmetric LV hypertrophy with no SAM/ LVOT narrowing.Diffuse interstitial LV myocardial fibrosis with raised native T1 values.CMR features are of hypertrophic cardiomyopathy with no obstruction. No myocardial inflammation/ infiltration/ infarction.",
      "STRESS CARDIAC MAGNETIC RESONANCE IMAGING (CMR)",
      "Indication | Known DVD with borderline LAD. For ischemia assessment.",
      "Findings | Low indexed LVEDV and normal indexed LVESV with LVEF of 60%. No LV hypertrophy is seen. Akinesia is seen in mid inferior segment. The RV is normal in appearance with preserved systolic function. No RV hypertrophy.   Normal atrial dimensions with mild MR (RF 10-15%) and TR. There was good physiological response to adenosine stress (140mcg/kg/min) with change of BP from 108/78 to 93/69 mm of Hg and heart rate from 80 to 110 bpm. The patient experienced breathlessness during the infusion, which resolved spontaneously on stopping the infusion. There is stress induced reversible perfusion defect seen in basal septal/ inferior wall, mid anterior/ septal/ inferolateral segments and apical anterior/ septal segments. On delayed enhancement imaging, transmural LGE is seen in mid inferior segment with sub endocardial LGE in basal inferior segment. No LV thrombus. Lungs and mediastinum are within normal limits. Few low intensity nodules are seen in both lobes of thyroid gland.",
      "(See graphs for BSA indexed LV values)",
      " | EDV (mL) | ESV (mL) | SV (mL) | EF (%) | Mass",
      "LV | 114 | 46 | 68 | 60 | 83",
      "Conclusion | Non dilated LV with LVEF of 60%.  Transmural infarct in mid inferior segment with sub endocardial infarct in basal inferior segment.Stress induced reversible ischemia in basal septal/inferior wall, mid anterior/septal/inferolateral segments and apical anterior/septal segments. CMR features are of ischemic non dilated cardiomyopathy. Of the 17 segments, 1 is non viable and 10 are viable/ hibernating. Ischemic burden of 55-60%.",
      "CARDIAC MAGNETIC RESONANCE IMAGING (CMR)",
      "Indication | Hypertrophic cardiomyopathy for further assessment.",
      "Findings | Normal indexed LVEDV and LVESV with LVEF of 72%. Asymmetric hypertrophy of the LV is seen predominantly involving the septum with basal anteroseptal segment measuring 20 mm in maximum end diastolic wall thickness. SAM of the anterior mitral leaflet is seen with narrowing of the LVOT and flow acceleration along the LVOT. No regional wall motion abnormality is seen.The RV is normal in appearance with preserved systolic function. No RV hypertrophy.  Dilated LA (iLA vol – 60 ml/m2) with mild to moderate MR (RF 25-30%). Normal right atrial dimensions with mild TR.T2FS images reveal no myocardial edema with normal T2 values (51 ms).On delayed enhancement imaging, no LV myocardial/ papillary muscle LGE is seen. No LV thrombus. T1 mapping reveals normal LV myocardial native T1 values (971 ms). Lungs and mediastinum are normal.",
      "(See graphs for BSA indexed LV values)",
      " | EDV (mL) | ESV (mL) | SV (mL) | EF (%) | Mass",
      "LV | 158 | 44 | 115 | 72 | 156",
      "Conclusion | Non-dilated LV with LVEF of 72%.Asymmetric LV hypertrophy with SAM and LVOT obstruction.No myocardial inflammation, infarction or infiltration.CMR features are of hypertrophic obstructive cardiomyopathy, likely non sarcomeric variant.",
      "HCM prognostic parameters",
      "Max thickness | 20 mm | >30mm poor prognosis",
      "Fibrotic burden | 0 % | >15% poor prognosis",
      "LVOT obstruction | Yes | ",
      "RV involvement | No | ",
      "Diastolic cavity obliteration/ LV apical aneurysm | No | ",
      "CARDIAC MAGNETIC RESONANCE IMAGING (CMR)",
      "Indication | Known LV dysfunction. For further assessment.",
      "Findings | Increased indexed LVEDV and LVESV with LVEF of 38%. No LV hypertrophy is seen. Diffuse severe global hypokinesia is seen with partial wall thinning in the lateral segments of LV Prominent LV trabeculations are seen in 10 out of 17 segments with a non compact to compact myocardial ratio of upto 3.Normal indexed RVEDV and RVESV with RVEF of 60%. No RV hypertrophy. No evidence of hypokinesia/ dyskinesia/ aneurysmal out pouching.   Dilated LA (iLA vol – 42 ml/m2) with mild MR (RF 10-15%). Normal RA dimensions with mild TR (RF 10-15%).T2 FS images reveal no obvious LV myocardial edema.On delayed enhancement imaging, diffuse sub epicardial to near transmural LGE is seen involving the lateral and inferior segments of LV from base to apex. Few areas of mid myocardial and sub epicardial LGE are also seen in the basal and mid anterior/ anteroseptal segments. LV myocardial fibrotic burden of 15%. No LV thrombus.Lungs and mediastinum are normal.",
      "(See graphs for BSA indexed LV/RV values)",
      " | EDV (mL) | ESV (mL) | SV (mL) | EF (%) | Mass (g)",
      "LV | 235 | 146 | 89 | 38 | 71",
      "RV | 154 | 62 | 92 | 60 | -",
      "Conclusion | Dilated LV with LVEF of 38%.Non-dilated RV with RVEF of 60%. Diffuse sub epicardial to transmural fibrosis in lateral/ inferior segments with mid myocardial fibrosis in basal/ mid anterior/ anteroseptal segments of LV.CMR features are of non ischemic dilated cardiomyopathy, likely due to post myocarditis sequalae/ sarcoidosis. No active inflammation at present."
