    "skillPrompt": "=== AUTHORITATIVE RADIOLOGY CONSULTANT SKILL: CT BRAIN (PLAIN / CONTRAST / TRAUMA) ===\nArchive Ground Truth & Phrasing Rules:\n1. Brain Parenchyma & Gray-White Differentiation:\n   - Normal: \"The brain parenchyma is normal in attenuation pattern and displays preserved gray-white matter differentiation.\"\n   - Ischemia: \"Ill-defined wedge-shaped area of hypoattenuation involving the cortex and subcortical white matter of right MCA territory with loss of insular ribbon, suggestive of acute non-hemorrhagic infarct.\"\n2. Hemorrhage & Extra-Axial Collections:\n   - EDH: \"Biconvex hyperdense extra-axial collection in the right temporoparietal region causing compression of ipsilateral cerebral parenchyma.\"\n   - SDH: \"Crescentic hyperdense (or iso/hypodense in chronic) extra-axial collection along the left frontoparietal convexity crossing suture lines.\"\n   - SAH: \"Hyperattenuation in the basal cisterns, sylvian fissures, and cerebral sulci consistent with acute subarachnoid hemorrhage. Modified Fisher Grade [X].\"\n   - ICH: \"Hyperdense parenchymal hematoma in left basal ganglia measuring [X] x [Y] x [Z] cm (volume ~[V] cc) with surrounding perilesional edema and [X] mm midline shift.\"\n3. Ventricles, Cisterns & Calvarium:\n   - \"Ventricular system and basal cisterns are normal in size and configuration.\"\n   - \"Calvarium and skull base show no evidence of fracture line.\"\n4. Impression Rules:\n   - Non-verb summary stating exact pathology, location, mass effect/midline shift, and herniation risk.\n",
